    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"3\">Level 3 - Intermediate</span><span class=\"time\">25 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip warn\">Medium</span><span class=\"chip accent\">Stack design</span><span class=\"chip accent\">Augmented data structure</span>\n    <a class=\"chip\" href=\"https://leetcode.com/problems/min-stack/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">LC 155</a>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Min Stack</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Let every stack entry remember the minimum of itself and everything under it. Then getMin is just a read of the top entry, and pop needs no repair, because the entry below already knows its own answer. All four operations O(1), O(n) space.</p>\n"
